    <heading level="1">Verbal</heading>
    <exercise number="1" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>What does it mean when a radical does not have an index? Is the expression equal to the radicand? Explain.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>When there is no index, it is assumed to be 2 or the square root. The expression would only be equal to the radicand if the index were 1.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="2" has_solution="false">
